  "code": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\"><title>Index / Studio — case-study starter</title><style>\n:root{--ink:#252324;--paper:#fffdf9;--accent:#7b304c;--line:#91868a;--wash:#f1e9ec}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font:1rem/1.7 system-ui,sans-serif}a{color:inherit;text-underline-offset:.3em}:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:5px}.skip{position:absolute;top:-6rem;left:1rem;background:white;padding:1rem}.skip:focus{top:1rem}.wrap{max-width:78rem;padding:clamp(1rem,4vw,3rem);margin:auto}header{display:flex;gap:1rem;justify-content:space-between;flex-wrap:wrap;border-bottom:1px solid var(--ink);padding-bottom:1rem}nav{display:flex;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap}.intro{padding:3rem 0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 2.2fr;gap:2rem}.label{font: .8rem/1.5 ui-monospace,monospace;color:var(--accent)}h1{font:400 clamp(2.8rem,6vw,5rem)/1.07 Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:0;max-width:18ch}.case{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 2.2fr;gap:2rem;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:2rem 0}.meta{margin:0}.meta dt{font:.8rem/1.5 ui-monospace,monospace;color:var(--accent);margin-top:1rem}.meta dd{margin:0}h2{font:400 2rem/1.2 Georgia,serif;margin:0 0 1rem}h3{font-size:1rem;margin-top:1.8rem}p{max-width:62ch}.visual{background:var(--wash);border:1px solid var(--line);padding:clamp(1rem,4vw,3rem);margin:2rem 0}.map{display:grid;grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr;gap:1rem}.map div{border:2px solid var(--accent);padding:1rem;min-height:5rem;display:flex;align-items:end;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace}.map .wide{grid-column:1/-1;min-height:8rem;background:var(--paper)}.map .narrow{background:#ddcad3}figcaption{font-size:.8rem;margin-top:1rem;color:#57434d}.decisions{list-style:none;padding:0;counter-reset:decision}.decisions li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:2rem 1fr;gap:.75rem;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:1rem 0;counter-increment:decision}.decisions li:before{content:counter(decision,decimal-leading-zero);color:var(--accent);font-family:ui-monospace,monospace}.closing{border-top:1px solid var(--ink);padding-top:2rem;max-width:60ch}footer{margin-top:3rem;color:#5d5458;font-size:.85rem}@media(max-width:48rem){.intro,.case{grid-template-columns:1fr}.meta{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem}.map{grid-template-columns:1fr}.map .wide{grid-column:auto}.map div{min-height:4rem}h1{max-width:20ch}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){*{animation:none!important;transition:none!important;scroll-behavior:auto!important}}\n</style></head><body><a class=\"skip\" href=\"#main\">Skip to case study</a><div class=\"wrap\"><header><strong>Index / Studio concept</strong><nav aria-label=\"Primary\"><a href=\"#case\">Selected study</a><a href=\"#adapt\">Adaptation notes</a></nav></header><main id=\"main\" tabindex=\"-1\"><section class=\"intro\" aria-labelledby=\"title\"><p class=\"label\">Portfolio starter<br>Fictional design exercise</p><h1 id=\"title\">Show the reasoning, not just the finish.</h1></section><article class=\"case\" id=\"case\" aria-labelledby=\"case-title\"><div><p class=\"label\">01 / Spatial information</p><dl class=\"meta\"><div><dt>Scope</dt><dd>Self-directed layout concept</dd></div><div><dt>Deliverable</dt><dd>Wayfinding composition</dd></div><div><dt>Status</dt><dd>Unvalidated prototype</dd></div><div><dt>Role</dt><dd>Replace with your actual contribution</dd></div></dl></div><div><h2 id=\"case-title\">A library without the guesswork</h2><p>A fictional brief: help a first-time visitor distinguish the quiet reading area, shared tables, and service desk before choosing a direction.</p><figure class=\"visual\"><div class=\"map\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Conceptual floor plan with a wide quiet area above shared tables and a narrow service desk\"><div class=\"wide\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Quiet reading</div><div aria-hidden=\"true\">Shared tables</div><div class=\"narrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Service desk</div></div><figcaption>Original CSS diagram. Spatial relationships are conceptual, not an architectural plan.</figcaption></figure><h3>Decisions worth explaining</h3><ol class=\"decisions\"><li><div><strong>One first question.</strong><br>Organize the entry point around the visitor's immediate choice, not the building's internal terminology.</div></li><li><div><strong>Words before decoration.</strong><br>Use specific labels and a consistent reading order; the accent color is supplementary.</div></li><li><div><strong>A visible next test.</strong><br>Ask participants to identify a destination, then record confusion before refining the diagram.</div></li></ol><h3>What remains unknown</h3><p>No usability study has been conducted for this sample. A real case study should distinguish observed findings from assumptions and describe accessibility constraints.</p></div></article><section class=\"closing\" id=\"adapt\" aria-labelledby=\"adapt-title\"><h2 id=\"adapt-title\">Make the evidence your own.</h2><p>Replace this fictional brief, diagram, role, and decisions with work you can share. Add project links only after checking permissions; do not imply a client relationship or an outcome you cannot support.</p></section></main><footer>Original composition starter · no personal profile, client logos, or external imagery.</footer></div></body></html>"
